From 0a6c44e0e194104946eba154727809ca019c7a40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:03:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Refine "Our Expertise": navy theme, white icons, scroll
 slide-in

Match the section background to the footer's navy-dark and give cards
a navy tone (instead of gray) so they read as part of the same dark
family. Drop the "Specialist capability..." subtitle. Remove the
per-card hyperlinks -- cards are now plain, non-clickable elements.
Bump card heading/body text size and weight so it reads clearly.
Icons switch from red to white.

Cards now slide in from the left as they scroll into view, reusing
the site's existing content-reveal scroll system (same
IntersectionObserver, no new one) with a horizontal slide-in variant
scoped to these cards, a staggered per-card delay, and its own faster
700ms pace so the entrance feels snappy rather than the slower 3s
pace the rest of the site's headings use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SjcntVjf5Nr2bdomgFdfPu
